A sign is refused: the text is digits only.

- Parameter base: The base, 2 to 36.
- Returns: `Maybe.Some(value)`, or `Maybe.None()` when the text is not a `u16` in that
  base, the value is out of range, or the base is outside 2 to 36.
- Example:
  ```sushi
  println("ff".parse_u16(16).realise(0))
  ```
:##
extend string parse_u16(i32 base) Maybe@(u16):
    match strict_digits(self, 0, base, 65535):
        Maybe.Some(v) -> return Maybe.Some(v as u16)
        Maybe.None -> return Maybe.None()

